    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d576">

                <pb facs="0695" n="635" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg635"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Gough to Mr.
                            Uhl</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Newport</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1895-06-13"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 13,
                    1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the State Department note
                    of the 23d January last, marked No. 17, requesting certain information with
                    regard to Canadian pelagic sealing in 1893 and 1894, I have the honor, acting
                    under the instructions of the Earl of Kimberley, to forward herewith copy of a
                    minute of the Canadian privy council containing the information asked for.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hugh Gough</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>












